# Slicer microVM sandboxes. The daemon runs as root and writes into whatever
# directory a slicer command is invoked from, so both of these appear in the
# repo the moment the VM workflow is driven from here: a root-owned .slicer/,
# and the VM's raw disk image -- 25GiB apparent, ~900MB sparse on disk.
#
# Neither is readable by the invoking user, which is worse than it sounds:
# `git add -A` fails outright on the image ("unable to index file"), and
# `git status` cannot even walk .slicer/. Ignoring them keeps the working tree
# usable if it happens again. The real fix is to run slicer from outside the
# repository.
.slicer/
**/.slicer/
*.img
# The VM agent's auth token. Root-owned and mode 600 here, so git could not have
# staged it -- but it is a credential written into the working directory, and it
# should be ignored on its own merits rather than by luck of the permissions.
vm_agent_secret

